From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slothfulchat <patches@slothfulchat.invalid>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 22:50:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sticker packs: store packs as blobs + tables, with JSON-RPC
 to manage them

Upstream keeps saved stickers as files in <account>/stickers/<pack>/,
outside the blobdir, so they are missing from backups and second-device
transfers, and saving a received sticker copies it. Packs are now rows in
slothfulchat_sticker_packs and stickers rows in slothfulchat_stickers
naming ordinary deduplicated blobs: saving a received sticker shares its
blob, and packs travel with the database.

- Tables are created with CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS, not a numbered
  migration, like the reply index: a fork-claimed version number would make
  a database skip upstream's real migration later.
- Housekeeping keeps every blob named in slothfulchat_stickers.
  test_housekeeping_keeps_sticker_pack_blobs fails if a rebase drops that
  query (checked by removing it) and also checks the blob goes once no pack
  holds it.
- Files added from disk are checked: extension png/webp/gif/tgs, the
  content's magic bytes must match it (the UI picks the renderer by
  extension), at most 5 MiB. Paths inside the blobdir are refused, because
  create_and_deduplicate would move them away from their message.
- The old stickers/ folders are moved in on first use, then removed.
- misc_get_stickers / misc_save_sticker keep their signatures and read and
  write the packs.
- New RPCs: get/create/rename/delete_sticker_pack, add_sticker_from_file,
  add_sticker_from_message, move/copy/remove_sticker,
  copy_sticker_pack_from_account (another profile's pack, deduplicated in
  the target), get_unsaved_sticker_messages (recent stickers in no pack;
  scans the newest 1000 sticker messages).
- Emojis per sticker: slothfulchat_sticker_emojis (blobname, emoji), keyed
  by image so moves, copies and other profiles' copies keep them; filled
  into Sticker.emojis by one extra query; set_sticker_emojis replaces the
  set (trimmed, deduped, at most 16 of at most 32 bytes).

FORK-ONLY: if upstream implements sticker packs, migrate these tables to
upstream's storage instead of keeping both.
